# Experiment C2 — results

Cost is instance CPU with the connector present minus the same workload with it absent, at each noise level. Both arms carry identical capture configuration, including supplemental logging, so only the connector differs.


## Measured cost by noise level

| Level | runs on/off | redo total (GB) | redo captured (GB) | redo discarded (GB) | CPU on (s) | CPU off (s) | **mining cost (s)** | events | A1 TPS |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 3/3 | 0.100 | 0.100 | 0.000 | 28.6 | 28.9 | **-0.2** | 27,000 | 50.0 |
| 1 | 3/3 | 0.621 | 0.621 | 0.000 | 33.8 | 28.4 | **5.4** | 27,000 | 50.0 |
| 2 | 3/3 | 1.133 | 1.134 | 0.000 | 39.5 | 32.7 | **6.8** | 27,003 | 50.0 |
| 3 | 3/3 | 2.169 | 2.163 | 0.005 | 49.0 | 40.0 | **9.0** | 17,384 | 49.5 |
| 4 | 3/3 | 3.712 | 3.715 | 0.000 | 79.7 | 49.6 | **30.2** | 26,532 | 49.0 |

## Manipulation checks

These decide whether the experiment measured what it intended to. A level that fails one of them is reported and excluded from the fit, not quietly retained.

* **Captured events constant across levels:** spread 35.6 % ✗ FAIL — noise leaked into the capture scope
* **A1 throughput constant across levels:** spread 1.9 % ✓ PASS
* **Total redo actually varied:** 0.100 → 3.712 GB (37.3×) ✓ PASS

## The fit

| Model | form | residual sum of squares |
|---|---|---|
| naive | cost = 7.1 · redo_captured | 58.03 |
| C2 | cost = -1,217.2 · redo_total + 1,224.3 · redo_captured | 5.53 |

* **a — CPU-seconds per GB of total redo:** -1,217.16 (95 % bootstrap CI -7,676.00 … 7,289.12)
* **b — additional CPU-seconds per GB of captured redo:** 1,224.35 (95 % CI -7,280.49 … 7,678.93)

**C2 is falsified by condition F-a.** The interval for the total-redo coefficient includes zero: on this evidence mining cost is explained by captured redo alone, and narrowing the capture scope does reduce database overhead proportionally. This is a result, and it should be reported as prominently as the alternative would have been.
